# "If the player chooses a permanent spell, the effect will apply to ... any damage dealt by the permanent that spell becomes
# when it resolves" (CR 609.7a). Bot2 casts Flametongue Kavu; in response Bot1 activates Jade Monolith targeting its Yoked Ox
# (0/4) and chooses the Kavu spell on the stack. The Kavu resolves and its enters ability deals 4 damage to the Ox: that is
# damage from the permanent the chosen spell became, so the Kavu deals it to Bot1 instead and the Ox lives. The effect is
# about a source that has since become another object, so it must outlive it.

